From: Ubuntu Desktop bug work
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: UpdateManager: do not call get_xid() on a NULL GdkWindow

show_settings() on X11 did self.get_window().get_xid() without checking
that the Gtk window was realized. After hide() or before map that is a
Python AttributeError and Settings never opens.

Forwarded: no
---
--- a/UpdateManager/UpdateManager.py
+++ b/UpdateManager/UpdateManager.py
@@ -206,7 +206,9 @@
                "--open-tab", str(page_number)]
 
         if "WAYLAND_DISPLAY" not in os.environ:
-            cmd += ["--toplevel", "%s" % self.get_window().get_xid()]
+            window = self.get_window()
+            if window is not None:
+                cmd += ["--toplevel", "%s" % window.get_xid()]
 
         try:
             p = Gio.Subprocess.new(cmd, Gio.SubprocessFlags.NONE)
